---
import Store from '../layouts/Store.astro';
import { perch } from '../data/perch';
---
<Store title="Privacy — Perch"><article class="shell section policy"><p class="eyebrow">Perch / Privacy</p><h1>A little less data.</h1><p>Last updated: October 14, 2026.</p><h2>This website</h2><p>This site does not include advertising trackers, analytics scripts, account registration, or a mailing-list form. Cloudflare hosts the site and may process technical request information, such as IP addresses, to deliver and protect it. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>The Mac app</h2><p>Perch is designed to keep agent activity and notes on your Mac. The current build stores events and notes locally, discards prompts, tool contents, and credentials, and makes no network requests. Your agent providers operate separately under their own policies.</p><h2>Payments</h2><p>Purchases are currently closed. When purchases open, checkout will be hosted by Stripe. Payment details will be entered on Stripe’s pages; this website does not receive card numbers. Stripe and the seller may process purchase and billing information needed to complete orders, provide support, and meet applicable recordkeeping obligations. See <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy">Stripe’s privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Support</h2><p>Support currently links to GitHub Issues. Issues are public: do not post credentials, private agent prompts, payment details, or personal information. GitHub processes information under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy policy</a>.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>For privacy questions, <a href={perch.support}>contact the project maintainers</a>.</p></article></Store>
<style>.policy{max-width:800px}.policy h1{font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,64px);margin:20px 0 30px}.policy h2{font-size:26px;margin:35px 0 14px}.policy p{color:var(--muted);margin:14px 0}.policy a{text-decoration:underline;text-underline-offset:3px}</style>
